From e79a1b37ec8461894de0a4cf927be2e51a38f1da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:40:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS fix round, track auth: sign-in limits,
 credential races, MFA re-enrolment, password cost, outbox purge

Findings of the ultracode re-check (rounds 1 and 2) fixed in edge-bff, each with its committed failing test now
passing:
- R1-3: EDGE_OWNER and EDGE_ADMIN_OWNERS may not be an owner key Orc reserves for its test key (golden-*, test-*,
  someone-else) or 'default'; edge-private still validates; the pattern is compared with Orc's.
- R1-7, R2-11, R2-12: a re-enrolment waits beside the confirmed authenticator (migration 20261119_011) and is
  swapped only by a code of the new one; a code confirms only the enrolment it was checked against; the MFA cap is
  decided, checked and counted under the enrolment's row lock.
- R1-8: failed reset codes counted per address for every address.
- R1-9, R1-16: the sign-in limit is per login and client address; per account at most 100 consecutive failed
  passwords (migration 20261119_010), answered as a wrong password while locked; a reset by email code lifts both;
  the limit's message says its own wait.
- R1-10: one HMAC label per throttle counter; REGISTER_HOUR/DAY share one; the password change has its own.
- R1-11, R1-12, R1-13, R1-14: the held registration cookie is kept; USERNAME_TAKEN uses a code try; a registration
  is mailed at most 3 times a day; the sign-in login takes the 254-character email bound.
- R2-9: credential writes and sessions made from a proof serialise on the account's users row and check the proof.
- R2-10: only code emails hold the next code back 60 s.
- R2-24, R2-35: outbox indexes for the hot reads and a SECURITY DEFINER purge of rows of addresses with no account
  (migration 20261119_012); the runtime still holds no DELETE on the outbox.
- R2-25: an outermost middleware answers unexpected exceptions 503 and logs class and SQLSTATE only.
- R2-29: scrypt N=2^14 r=8 p=5 with a versioned verifier; old verifiers check at the same cost and are rehashed at
  the next sign-in.
- R2-37: password work runs on its own pool with an admission limit (503 with Retry-After).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015yBxadqbqnpdpSwmfCDQca
